.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tine-run-end 1  "end " 
.SH NAME
tine\-run\-end \- Squash the run into one commit when none of it is pushed, branched or interleaved with other commits; otherwise leave it as it is
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine run end\fR [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-graph\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIRUN\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Squash the run into one commit when none of it is pushed, branched or interleaved with other commits; otherwise leave it as it is
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
Subject of the squashed commit
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<GRAPH>\fR
The graph. Defaults to $TINE_GRAPH, else the graph folder around the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the typed result (schema tine.cli/1) as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIRUN\fR>

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTINE_RUN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
